vement, the lower hall's glass wall onto the Villa Reale's garden; the plate widened to take Via Palestro across its width and the Giardini Indro Montanelli north of it (lawn, a path, rows of planes and limes); the Villa Reale's west wing given its three storeys of windows. Still guessed: the outlines here are sparse (only a fragment of the PAC is drawn, the Villa Reale's wing appears 2-3 storeys further east), so the exact footprint and the east-west position are not confirmed by them; the trapezoid, the levels' heights and the tile colour remain as first guessed."}